# Generators (JSON, WASM, HTTP)

How to run: `docs/run-example.md`. Build: `docs/build.md`. How the page is produced: `docs/frontend.md`.

**JSON (`src/json.zig`, module `zigma_json`):** imports `zigma` only. `stringifyRecord` / `stringifyRecords` follow Zig field types (string, int, bool, nested struct); `stringifyRecordSchema(completeRecord(...))` writes `[{"name","label"},...]`; `stringifyEntitySchema` / `stringifyEntityCatalog` write entity Infos (`name`, `pk`, `uks`, `fks`, `fields` with `name`/`label`/`type`/`storage`). `storage` is the Zig shape (`text`/`integer`/`boolean`/`date`/`object`); a struct of three integers is `date`. Test: `test/json_test.zig` (aida plus `test/tiny_system.zig`).

**WASM (`src/frontend/main.zig`):** `wasm32-freestanding`, `entry = .disabled`, `rdynamic`, exports memory. Imports `zigma`, `zigma_json`, and a `system` module (`type_defs`, `entity_defs`). Catalog from `stringifyEntityCatalog` (`schema_ptr`, `schema_len`). Packed strings in `input_buf`, per-field lengths in `lengths_buf`; `build_row(entity_index)` / `create_row(entity_index)` parse into `RecordInstanceType` of that entity's `.fields`. `create_row` calls `env.js_send_post` with the JSON. `json_ptr` / `json_len` expose the last built row for PUT.

**JS (`src/frontend/main.js`):** after WASM load, parses the catalog, builds a nav of entity names (hash, else first catalog entity), one `#sheet-table` (thead labels from entity.fields, tfoot empty alta row, tbody from `GET /{entity}`). Post packs field values and calls `create_row`; Save on an existing row calls `build_row` and `PUT /{entity}`. Input type follows field `storage` (`integer`/`boolean`/`date`/text). On success GETs again.

**HTTP (`src/http/main.zig`):** listens `0.0.0.0:8080`, CORS `*`. In-memory JSON list per `system.entity_defs` name. Optional `system.seeds` (row arrays keyed by entity name). `GET /{entity}` returns the list. `POST /{entity}` parses a record instance, appends. `PUT /{entity}` replaces the row whose pk matches. Replies `{"status": "received"}`. Other paths → 404. From `examples/aida/`: `zig build backend` runs it (`dummy` is an alias).

The example app `examples/aida/` calls `addAppFromDep` with `src/system.zig` as `system`. From that directory: `zig build` writes `zig-out/frontend/` (`frontend.wasm`, `main.js`, `index.html`) and `zig-out/bin/backend`. `zig build backend` runs it (`dummy` is an alias).
